{"format": 1, "id": "tceGOgy52xEcP-pHKATGPQ", "title": "Simplifying parse_tree", "frame": "landscape", "theme": "dark", "tokens": {}, "status": "finished", "questions": ["Why not split the depth rules into a helper now?", "How do the tree tests cover the dedupe order?"], "notes": {}, "slides": [{"id": "simplifying-parse-tree", "rev": 1, "kind": "title", "title": "Simplifying parse_tree", "classes": [], "shown": "src/showntell/kinds.py", "visual": {}, "says": [{"id": "simplifying-parse-tree.1.1", "status": "ready", "text": "The tree parser does three jobs in one 45-line function. We'll pull them apart, one small edit at a time.", "cues": [], "notes": [], "code": [], "audio": "audio/fda92376516eefe5eee719fd.mp3", "duration": 7.45, "words": [{"s": 0.25, "e": 0.325, "c0": 0, "c1": 3}, {"s": 0.325, "e": 0.55, "c0": 4, "c1": 8}, {"s": 0.55, "e": 1.0, "c0": 9, "c1": 15}, {"s": 1.0, "e": 1.262, "c0": 16, "c1": 20}, {"s": 1.262, "e": 1.538, "c0": 21, "c1": 26}, {"s": 1.538, "e": 2.0, "c0": 27, "c1": 31}, {"s": 2.0, "e": 2.15, "c0": 32, "c1": 34}, {"s": 2.15, "e": 2.413, "c0": 35, "c1": 38}, {"s": 2.413, "e": 3.325, "c0": 39, "c1": 46}, {"s": 3.325, "e": 4.15, "c0": 47, "c1": 55}, {"s": 4.275, "e": 4.425, "c0": 57, "c1": 62}, {"s": 4.425, "e": 4.638, "c0": 63, "c1": 67}, {"s": 4.638, "e": 4.775, "c0": 68, "c1": 72}, {"s": 4.775, "e": 5.325, "c0": 73, "c1": 78}, {"s": 5.438, "e": 5.713, "c0": 80, "c1": 83}, {"s": 5.713, "e": 6.1, "c0": 84, "c1": 89}, {"s": 6.1, "e": 6.375, "c0": 90, "c1": 94}, {"s": 6.375, "e": 6.463, "c0": 95, "c1": 97}, {"s": 6.463, "e": 6.525, "c0": 98, "c1": 99}, {"s": 6.525, "e": 7.2, "c0": 100, "c1": 104}]}]}, {"id": "three-jobs", "rev": 1, "kind": "code", "title": "Three jobs in one loop", "classes": [], "shown": "", "visual": {"lang": "python", "code": "def parse_tree(body: str, attrs: dict) -> tuple[dict, list[str]]:\n    \"\"\"```tree: one entry per line, nested by indentation (two or four spaces) or by `tree` output\n    (\u251c\u2500\u2500 \u2514\u2500\u2500 \u2502). A trailing / or deeper lines below mark a folder; `# text` after an entry is a note.\"\"\"\n    rows, problems = [], []\n    unit = None\n    for raw in body.split(\"\\n\"):\n        if not raw.strip():\n            continue\n        raw = raw.rstrip()\n        m = TREE_RE.match(raw)\n        lead, rest = m.group(1), m.group(2).strip()\n        if re.match(r\"^[\\s\u2502|]*[\u251c\u2514`]\", raw):  # drawn by `tree`\n            depth = len(re.findall(r\"[\u2502|]\\s{1,3}|\\s{4}\", lead)) + 1\n        else:\n            spaces = len(raw) - len(raw.lstrip(\" \"))\n            if spaces and unit is None:\n                unit = spaces\n            depth = spaces // (unit or 2)\n        note = \"\"\n        if \" #\" in rest:\n            rest, _, note = rest.partition(\" #\")\n            rest, note = rest.strip(), note.strip()\n        if rest and rest != \".\":\n            rows.append([depth, rest, note])\n    if rows:\n        base = min(r[0] for r in rows)\n        for r in rows:\n            r[0] -= base\n    items, stack = [], []\n    for i, (depth, name, note) in enumerate(rows):\n        folder = name.endswith(\"/\") or (i + 1 < len(rows) and rows[i + 1][0] > depth)\n        if depth > len(stack):\n            problems.append(f\"`{name}` is indented deeper than the entry above it\")\n            depth = len(stack)\n        del stack[depth:]\n        clean = name.rstrip(\"/\")\n        items.append({\"id\": \"/\".join([*stack, clean]), \"name\": clean + (\"/\" if folder else \"\"), \"depth\": depth,\n                      \"folder\": folder, \"note\": note})\n        if folder:\n            stack.append(clean)\n    seen: set[str] = set()\n    for it in items:\n        while it[\"id\"] in seen:\n            it[\"id\"] += \"~\"\n        seen.add(it[\"id\"])\n    return {\"items\": items, \"ids\": [it[\"id\"] for it in items], \"title\": attrs.get(\"title\", \"\")}, problems\n", "start": 204, "title": "kinds.py", "file": "src/showntell/kinds.py", "scroll": true}, "says": [{"id": "three-jobs.1.1", "status": "ready", "text": "First, the scan loop turns each line into a depth, a name and a note. It also guesses the indent unit.", "cues": [{"at": 7, "end": 20, "label": "the scan loop", "target": "L209-227", "text": "", "kind": "lines", "side": "new", "l0": 209, "l1": 227, "t": 0.725}], "notes": [], "code": [], "audio": "audio/bcf169f2e8ea66d5ae7e9cbe.mp3", "duration": 6.975, "words": [{"s": 0.3, "e": 0.675, "c0": 0, "c1": 5}, {"s": 0.725, "e": 0.838, "c0": 7, "c1": 10}, {"s": 0.838, "e": 1.175, "c0": 11, "c1": 15}, {"s": 1.175, "e": 1.4, "c0": 16, "c1": 20}, {"s": 1.4, "e": 1.712, "c0": 21, "c1": 26}, {"s": 1.712, "e": 2.0, "c0": 27, "c1": 31}, {"s": 2.0, "e": 2.288, "c0": 32, "c1": 36}, {"s": 2.288, "e": 2.487, "c0": 37, "c1": 41}, {"s": 2.487, "e": 2.575, "c0": 42, "c1": 43}, {"s": 2.575, "e": 3.15, "c0": 44, "c1": 49}, {"s": 3.263, "e": 3.388, "c0": 51, "c1": 52}, {"s": 3.388, "e": 3.85, "c0": 53, "c1": 57}, {"s": 3.85, "e": 3.962, "c0": 58, "c1": 61}, {"s": 3.962, "e": 4.025, "c0": 62, "c1": 63}, {"s": 4.025, "e": 4.675, "c0": 64, "c1": 68}, {"s": 4.8, "e": 4.938, "c0": 70, "c1": 72}, {"s": 4.938, "e": 5.275, "c0": 73, "c1": 77}, {"s": 5.275, "e": 5.662, "c0": 78, "c1": 85}, {"s": 5.662, "e": 5.8, "c0": 86, "c1": 89}, {"s": 5.8, "e": 6.125, "c0": 90, "c1": 96}, {"s": 6.125, "e": 6.725, "c0": 97, "c1": 101}]}, {"id": "three-jobs.2.1", "status": "ready", "text": "Second, the rebase shifts depths so the shallowest entry is zero.", "cues": [{"at": 8, "end": 18, "label": "the rebase", "target": "L228-231", "text": "", "kind": "lines", "side": "new", "l0": 228, "l1": 231, "t": 0.713}], "notes": [], "code": [], "audio": "audio/0dccf2f38abdfff87b920e6e.mp3", "duration": 4.375, "words": [{"s": 0.3, "e": 0.675, "c0": 0, "c1": 6}, {"s": 0.713, "e": 0.8, "c0": 8, "c1": 11}, {"s": 0.8, "e": 1.2, "c0": 12, "c1": 18}, {"s": 1.2, "e": 1.538, "c0": 19, "c1": 25}, {"s": 1.538, "e": 2.25, "c0": 26, "c1": 32}, {"s": 2.25, "